perform_menu_item DEV TOOL (absent from Distribution builds). Run a main-menu item by its path, e.g. ["File", "Export…"], in a project's window — delivered to that window's own responder chain, so it works with the app inactive and its window behind others — and answer after the app settles (a sheet or window that arrives a moment later is in the answer; bounded at 3 s). It is what puts a sheet, the Settings window or a panel up for snapshot_ui. Refused, by name and running nothing: a disabled item, a submenu, an ['path', 'project']
play_preview DEV TOOL (absent from Distribution builds). Play a project's preview forward for seconds at rate (1, 2 or 4) through the transport's own calls, then pause, and answer how much of it the compositor composed: from and to (ticks), rate, wall_seconds, frame_ticks, frames_expected (the frames from from — or from seek_to — up to to), frames_composed (how many of those the compositor finished), composed_ratio, and compose_ms {mean, p95, worst} over every frame it served. It pauses first and waits up to ['stale_armed', 'rate', 'stale_ticks', 'digests', 'project', 'seconds', 'seek_to']
